## 🎯 About The Project

NEXUS is an enterprise-grade, multi-chain **x402 Payment Verification & Settlement Mesh**. It operates as an open, non-custodial middleware layer that sits perfectly between API Resource Servers (such as streaming platforms, SaaS tools, or AI agent networks) and blockchain settlement networks.

By exploiting **Algorand's sub-3-second deterministic finality** and **native atomic transaction groups**, NEXUS successfully eliminates the latency, high fees, and atomicity issues common in standard EVM-based x402 facilitators—without requiring the deployment of smart contracts.

> **Note:** The Netflix web application included in this repository acts purely as a **demonstration Resource Server** to visually prove the end-to-end functionality of the underlying NEXUS Settlement Mesh.

---

## ✨ Key Features

<table align="center">
  <tr>
    <td align="center">⚡<br/><b>Deterministic Finality</b><br/>Validates blocks under 3 seconds without Reorg risks.</td>
    <td align="center">🛡️<br/><b>Non-Custodial Design</b><br/>Never requests or holds private keys/seed phrases.</td>
    <td align="center">🔗<br/><b>Atomic Composability</b><br/>Payment transfers and receipts succeed or fail together natively.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td align="center">🚦<br/><b>Circuit Breaker Routing</b><br/>Dynamic failover using a strict closed/open/half-open mesh.</td>
    <td align="center">🔐<br/><b>Replay Protection</b><br/>Dual-layer Redis idempotency locking prevents duplicate settlements.</td>
    <td align="center">📄<br/><b>Off-chain Receipts</b><br/>HMAC-SHA256 verification and PDF invoice generation.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

